From 218f0d20ee72c0be11ec6fec88dc3cbed56125d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron Morgan <morganaaron.mail@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:55:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] 3DS: queueable sources, PNG, shared CFNT, thread bit, tiled
 ImageData, safe texture frees, worker scheduling

- love.audio.newQueueableSource was an empty stub and not registered; implement it
  and the ndsp-backed queue (slots, pending submit on play, starvation stop)
- clamp the queue constructor's buffer count (it overran a 2-slot array)
- register PNGHandler on 3DS so love.graphics.newImage loads .png
- static sources freed their shared SoundData buffer in the destructor
- restore setVolume after ndspChnReset on play
- share one refcounted system-font (CFNT) copy between fonts
- open the bit library in love.thread workers
- ImageData decode/encode converts to and from the GPU's tiled RGBA8 layout
- free textures and render targets after the frame ends: citro3d panics when a
  render target is deleted mid-frame, which Lua's GC did (console crash)
- refresh the viewport and projection on every render-target switch: a
  400x240 canvas matched the cached top-screen rect and kept the screen
  projection (game picture off-centre)
- run love.thread workers on core 2 (New 3DS), else one priority above the
  main thread: equal priorities on one core starved them (audio dropouts)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
